///
/// If this is set to a number, it represents Hz, so "60" means try to iterate 60 times per second. "0" means to iterate as fast as possible. Negative values are illegal, but reserved, in case they are useful in a future revision of SDL.
/// There are other strings that have special meaning. If set to "waitevent", SDL_AppIterate (C macro outside this module) will not be called until new event(s) have arrived (and been processed by SDL_AppEvent (C macro outside this module)). This can be useful for apps that are completely idle except in response to input.
/// On some platforms, or if you are using SDL_main (C API outside this module) instead of SDL_AppIterate (C macro outside this module), this hint is ignored. When the hint can be used, it is allowed to be changed at any time.
