/// Compose a custom blend mode for renderers.
///
/// The functions render.Renderer.setRenderDrawBlendMode and render.setTextureBlendMode accept the blendmode.BlendMode returned by this function if the renderer supports it.
/// A blend mode controls how the pixels from a drawing operation (source) get combined with the pixels from the render target (destination). First, the components of the source and destination pixels get multiplied with their blend factors. Then, the blend operation takes the two products and calculates the result that will get stored in the render target.
/// Expressed in pseudocode, it would look like this:
/// ```c
/// dstRGB=colorOperation(srcRGB*srcColorFactor,dstRGB*dstColorFactor);
/// dstA=alphaOperation(srcA*srcAlphaFactor,dstA*dstAlphaFactor);
/// ```
///
/// Where the functions `colorOperation(src, dst)` and `alphaOperation(src,
/// dst)` can return one of the following:
/// - `src + dst`
/// - `src - dst`
/// - `dst - src`
/// - `min(src, dst)`
/// - `max(src, dst)`
/// The red, green, and blue components are always multiplied with the first, second, and third components of the blendmode.BlendFactor, respectively. The fourth component is not used.
/// The alpha component is always multiplied with the fourth component of the blendmode.BlendFactor. The other components are not used in the alpha calculation.
/// Support for these blend modes varies for each renderer. To check if a specific blendmode.BlendMode is supported, create a renderer and pass it to either render.Renderer.setRenderDrawBlendMode or render.setTextureBlendMode. They will return with an error if the blend mode is not supported.
/// This list describes the support of custom blend modes for each renderer. All renderers support the four blend modes listed in the blendmode.BlendMode enumeration.
/// - **direct3d**: Supports all operations with all factors. However, some factors produce unexpected results with `blendmode.BlendOperation.minimum` and `blendmode.BlendOperation.maximum`.
/// - **direct3d11**: Same as Direct3D 9.
/// - **opengl**: Supports the `blendmode.BlendOperation.add` operation with all factors. OpenGL versions 1.1, 1.2, and 1.3 do not work correctly here.
/// - **opengles2**: Supports the `blendmode.BlendOperation.add`, `blendmode.BlendOperation.subtract`, `blendmode.BlendOperation.rev_subtract` operations with all factors.
/// - **psp**: No custom blend mode support.
/// - **software**: No custom blend mode support.
/// Some renderers do not provide an alpha component for the default render target. The `blendmode.BlendFactor.dst_alpha` and `blendmode.BlendFactor.one_minus_dst_alpha` factors do not have an effect in this case.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `src_color_factor`: the blendmode.BlendFactor applied to the red, green, and blue components of the source pixels.
///   - `dst_color_factor`: the blendmode.BlendFactor applied to the red, green, and blue components of the destination pixels.
///   - `color_operation`: the blendmode.BlendOperation used to combine the red, green, and blue components of the source and destination pixels.
///   - `src_alpha_factor`: the blendmode.BlendFactor applied to the alpha component of the source pixels.
///   - `dst_alpha_factor`: the blendmode.BlendFactor applied to the alpha component of the destination pixels.
///   - `alpha_operation`: the blendmode.BlendOperation used to combine the alpha component of the source and destination pixels.
///
/// - **Returns:** an blendmode.BlendMode that represents the chosen factors and operations.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** render.Renderer.setRenderDrawBlendMode
/// - **See also:** render.Renderer.getRenderDrawBlendMode
/// - **See also:** render.setTextureBlendMode
/// - **See also:** render.getTextureBlendMode
inline fn composeCustomBlendMode(src_color_factor: BlendFactor, dst_color_factor: BlendFactor, color_operation: BlendOperation, src_alpha_factor: BlendFactor, dst_alpha_factor: BlendFactor, alpha_operation: BlendOperation) BlendMode {
    return c.SDL_ComposeCustomBlendMode(@intCast(@intFromEnum(src_color_factor)), @intCast(@intFromEnum(dst_color_factor)), @intCast(@intFromEnum(color_operation)), @intCast(@intFromEnum(src_alpha_factor)), @intCast(@intFromEnum(dst_alpha_factor)), @intCast(@intFromEnum(alpha_operation)));
}

/// Convert some audio data of one format to another format.
///
/// Please note that this function is for convenience, but should not be used to resample audio in blocks, as it will introduce audio artifacts on the boundaries. You should only use this function if you are converting audio data in its entirety in one call. If you want to convert audio in smaller chunks, use an audio.Stream, which is designed for this situation.
/// Internally, this function creates and destroys an audio.Stream on each use, so it's also less efficient than using one directly, if you need to convert multiple times.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `src_spec`: the format details of the input audio.
///   - `src_data`: the audio data to be converted.
///   - `dst_spec`: the format details of the output audio.
///
/// - **Returns:** true on success or false on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// Call `convertAudioSamples`, copy its SDL-owned audio buffer, and return allocator-backed data.
inline fn convertAudioSamples(allocator_: std.mem.Allocator, src_spec: ?*const AudioSpec, src_data: []const u8, dst_spec: ?*const AudioSpec) Error![]u8 {
    const DataPointer = @typeInfo(@typeInfo(@TypeOf(c.SDL_ConvertAudioSamples)).@"fn".params[4].type.?).pointer.child;
    const Length = @typeInfo(@typeInfo(@TypeOf(c.SDL_ConvertAudioSamples)).@"fn".params[5].type.?).pointer.child;
    var data_raw: DataPointer = null;
    var length_raw: Length = 0;
    if (!c.SDL_ConvertAudioSamples(@ptrCast(src_spec), @ptrCast(src_data.ptr), @intCast(src_data.len), @ptrCast(dst_spec), &data_raw, &length_raw)) return error.SdlFailure;
    const output_source = data_raw;
    if (output_source == null) return error.SdlFailure;
    defer c.SDL_free(@ptrCast(output_source));
    const length = std.math.cast(usize, length_raw) orelse return error.SdlFailure;
    const data = allocator_.alloc(u8, length) catch return error.OutOfMemory;
    @memcpy(data, @as([*]const u8, @ptrCast(output_source))[0..length]);
    return data;
}

/// Convert the coordinates in an event to render coordinates.
///
/// This takes into account several states:
/// - The window dimensions.
/// - The logical presentation settings (render.Renderer.setRenderLogicalPresentation)
