/// - **See also:** gpu.createShader
/// - **See also:** gpu.bindGraphicsPipeline
/// - **See also:** gpu.GraphicsPipeline.deinit
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn createGpuGraphicsPipeline(device: ?GpuDevice, createinfo: ?*const GpuGraphicsPipelineCreateInfo) Error!GpuGraphicsPipeline {
    const result = c.SDL_CreateGPUGraphicsPipeline(if (device) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, @ptrCast(createinfo));
    if (result == null) return error.SdlFailure;
    return GpuGraphicsPipeline{ .value = @ptrCast(result.?), .parent = (device orelse return error.SdlFailure) };
}

/// Create a 2D GPU rendering context.
///
/// The GPU device to use is passed in as a parameter. If this is NULL, then a device will be created normally and can be retrieved using render.Renderer.getGpuDevice().
/// The window to use is passed in as a parameter. If this is NULL, then this will become an offscreen renderer. In that case, you should call render.Renderer.setRenderTarget() to setup rendering to a texture, and then call render.Renderer.renderPresent() normally to complete drawing a frame.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `device`: the GPU device to use with the renderer, or NULL to create a device.
///   - `window`: the window where rendering is displayed, or NULL to create an offscreen renderer.
///
/// - **Returns:** a valid rendering context or NULL if there was an error; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** If this function is called with a valid GPU device, it should be called on the thread that created the device. If this function is called with a valid window, it should be called on the thread that created the window.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.4.0.
/// - **See also:** render.createRendererWithProperties
/// - **See also:** render.Renderer.getGpuDevice
/// - **See also:** gpu.createShader
/// - **See also:** render.createGpuState
/// - **See also:** render.Renderer.setGpuRenderState
inline fn createGpuRenderer(device: ?GpuDevice, window: ?Window) ?Renderer {
    const result = c.SDL_CreateGPURenderer(if (device) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, if (window) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null);
    return if (result) |value| Renderer{ .value = @ptrCast(value) } else null;
}

/// Create custom GPU render state.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `renderer`: the renderer to use.
///   - `createinfo`: a struct describing the GPU render state to create.
///
/// - **Returns:** a custom GPU render state or NULL on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
