/// Get the underlying joystick from a gamepad.
///
/// This function will give you a joystick.Joystick object, which allows you to use the joystick.Joystick functions with a gamepad.Gamepad object. This would be useful for getting a joystick's position at any given time, even if it hasn't moved (moving it would produce an event, which would have the axis' value).
/// The pointer returned is owned by the gamepad.Gamepad. You should not call joystick.Joystick.close() on it, for example, since doing so will likely cause SDL to crash.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `gamepad_2`: the gamepad object that you want to get a joystick from.
///
/// - **Returns:** an joystick.Joystick object, or NULL on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn getGamepadJoystick(gamepad_2: ?Gamepad) Error!Joystick {
    const result = c.SDL_GetGamepadJoystick(if (gamepad_2) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null);
    if (result == null) return error.SdlFailure;
    return Joystick{ .value = @ptrCast(result.?) };
}

