/// Get a snapshot of the current state of the keyboard.
///
/// A array element with a value of true means that the key is pressed and a value of false means that it is not. Indexes into this array are obtained by using scancode.Scancode values.
/// Use events.pump() to update the state array.
/// This function gives you the current state after all events have been processed, so if a key or button has been pressed and released before you process events, then the pressed state will never show up in the keyboard.getState() calls.
/// Note: This function doesn't take into account whether shift has been pressed or not.
///
/// - **Returns:** a pointer to an array of key states.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** events.pump
/// - **See also:** keyboard.reset
///
/// The returned slice is borrowed from SDL. Do not free it, and observe the upstream lifetime rules above.
inline fn getKeyboardState() []const bool {
    var count: @typeInfo(@typeInfo(@TypeOf(c.SDL_GetKeyboardState)).@"fn".params[0].type.?).pointer.child = 0;
    const result = c.SDL_GetKeyboardState(&count);
    if (result == null) return &.{};
    const length = std.math.cast(usize, count) orelse return &.{};
    return @as([*]const bool, @ptrCast(result))[0..length];
}

