/// Get the properties associated with a renderer.
///
/// The following read-only properties are provided by SDL:
/// - `render.prop_renderer_name_string`: the name of the rendering driver
/// - `render.prop_renderer_window_pointer`: the window where rendering is displayed, if any
/// - `render.prop_renderer_surface_pointer`: the surface where rendering is displayed, if this is a software renderer without a window
/// - `render.prop_renderer_vsync_number`: the current vsync setting
/// - `render.prop_renderer_max_texture_size_number`: the maximum texture width and height
/// - `render.prop_renderer_texture_formats_pointer`: a (const pixels.PixelFormat *) array of pixel formats, terminated with pixels.PixelFormat.unknown, representing the available texture formats for this renderer.
/// - `render.prop_renderer_texture_wrapping_boolean`: true if the renderer supports render.TextureAddressMode.wrap on non-power-of-two textures.
/// - `render.prop_renderer_output_colorspace_number`: an pixels.Colorspace value describing the colorspace for output to the display, defaults to pixels.Colorspace.srgb.
/// - `render.prop_renderer_hdr_enabled_boolean`: true if the output colorspace is pixels.Colorspace.srgb_linear and the renderer is showing on a display with HDR enabled. This property can change dynamically when events.EventType.window_hdr_state_changed is sent.
/// - `render.prop_renderer_sdr_white_point_float`: the value of SDR white in the pixels.Colorspace.srgb_linear colorspace. When HDR is enabled, this value is automatically multiplied into the color scale. This property can change dynamically when events.EventType.window_hdr_state_changed is sent.
/// - `render.prop_renderer_hdr_headroom_float`: the additional high dynamic range that can be displayed, in terms of the SDR white point. When HDR is not enabled, this will be 1.0. This property can change dynamically when events.EventType.window_hdr_state_changed is sent.
/// With the direct3d renderer:
/// - `render.prop_renderer_d3d9_device_pointer`: the IDirect3DDevice9 associated with the renderer
/// With the direct3d11 renderer:
/// - `render.prop_renderer_d3d11_device_pointer`: the ID3D11Device associated with the renderer
/// - `render.prop_renderer_d3d11_swapchain_pointer`: the IDXGISwapChain1 associated with the renderer. This may change when the window is resized.
/// With the direct3d12 renderer:
/// - `render.prop_renderer_d3d12_device_pointer`: the ID3D12Device associated with the renderer
/// - `render.prop_renderer_d3d12_swapchain_pointer`: the IDXGISwapChain4 associated with the renderer.
/// - `render.prop_renderer_d3d12_command_queue_pointer`: the ID3D12CommandQueue associated with the renderer
/// With the vulkan renderer:
/// - `render.prop_renderer_vulkan_instance_pointer`: the VkInstance associated with the renderer
/// - `render.prop_renderer_vulkan_surface_number`: the VkSurfaceKHR associated with the renderer
/// - `render.prop_renderer_vulkan_physical_device_pointer`: the VkPhysicalDevice associated with the renderer
/// - `render.prop_renderer_vulkan_device_pointer`: the VkDevice associated with the renderer
/// - `render.prop_renderer_vulkan_graphics_queue_family_index_number`: the queue family index used for rendering
/// - `render.prop_renderer_vulkan_present_queue_family_index_number`: the queue family index used for presentation
/// - `render.prop_renderer_vulkan_swapchain_image_count_number`: the number of swapchain images, or potential frames in flight, used by the Vulkan renderer
/// With the gpu renderer:
/// - `render.prop_renderer_gpu_device_pointer`: the gpu.Device associated with the renderer
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `renderer`: the rendering context.
///
/// - **Returns:** a valid property ID on success or 0 on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn getRendererProperties(renderer: ?Renderer) Error!PropertiesId {
    const result = c.SDL_GetRendererProperties(if (renderer) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null);
    if (result == 0) return error.SdlFailure;
    return result;
}

