/// Get a human-readable name for a scancode.
///
/// **Warning**: The returned name is by design not stable across platforms, e.g. the name for `scancode.Scancode.scancode_lgui` is "Left GUI" under Linux but "Left
/// Windows" under Microsoft Windows, and some scancodes like `scancode.Scancode.scancode_nonusbackslash` don't have any name at all. There are even scancodes that share names, e.g. `scancode.Scancode.scancode_return` and `scancode.Scancode.scancode_return2` (both called "Return"). This function is therefore unsuitable for creating a stable cross-platform two-way mapping between strings and scancodes.
