/// Gets a previously created tray entry submenu.
///
/// You should have called tray.createSubmenu() on the entry object. This function allows you to fetch it again later.
/// This function does the same thing as tray.Tray.getMenu(), except that it takes a tray.Entry instead of a tray.Tray.
/// A menu does not need to be destroyed; it will be destroyed with the tray.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
