///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `size`: the size to allocate.
///
/// - **Returns:** a pointer to the allocated memory, or NULL if allocation failed.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** stdinc.free
/// - **See also:** stdinc.calloc
/// - **See also:** stdinc.realloc
/// - **See also:** stdinc.alignedAlloc
inline fn malloc(size: c_ulong) ?*anyopaque {
    const result = c.SDL_malloc(size);
    return if (result == null) null else @ptrCast(result);
}

/// Maps a transfer buffer into application address space.
///
/// You must unmap the transfer buffer before encoding upload commands. The memory is owned by the graphics driver - do NOT call stdinc.free() on the returned pointer.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `device`: a GPU context.
///   - `transfer_buffer`: a transfer buffer.
///   - `cycle`: if true, cycles the transfer buffer if it is already bound.
///
/// - **Returns:** the address of the mapped transfer buffer memory, or NULL on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn mapGpuTransferBuffer(device: ?GpuDevice, transfer_buffer: ?GpuTransferBuffer, cycle: bool) Error!*anyopaque {
    const result = c.SDL_MapGPUTransferBuffer(if (device) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, if (transfer_buffer) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, cycle);
    if (result == null) return error.SdlFailure;
    return @ptrCast(result.?);
}

/// Map an RGB triple to an opaque pixel value for a given pixel format.
///
/// This function maps the RGB color value to the specified pixel format and returns the pixel value best approximating the given RGB color value for the given pixel format.
/// If the format has a palette (8-bit) the index of the closest matching color in the palette will be returned.
/// If the specified pixel format has an alpha component it will be returned as all 1 bits (fully opaque).
/// If the pixel format bpp (color depth) is less than 32-bpp then the unused upper bits of the return value can safely be ignored (e.g., with a 16-bpp format the return value can be assigned to a Uint16, and similarly a Uint8 for an 8-bpp format).
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `format`: a pointer to pixels.PixelFormatDetails describing the pixel format.
///   - `palette`: an optional palette for indexed formats, may be NULL.
///   - `r`: the red component of the pixel in the range 0-255.
///   - `g`: the green component of the pixel in the range 0-255.
///   - `b`: the blue component of the pixel in the range 0-255.
///
/// - **Returns:** a pixel value.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread, as long as the palette is not modified.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** pixels.getPixelFormatDetails
