/// Start an async read.
///
/// This function reads up to `size` bytes from `offset` position in the data source to the area pointed at by `ptr`. This function may read less bytes than requested.
/// This function returns as quickly as possible; it does not wait for the read to complete. On a successful return, this work will continue in the background. If the work begins, even failure is asynchronous: a failing return value from this function only means the work couldn't start at all.
/// `ptr` must remain available until the work is done, and may be accessed by the system at any time until then. Do not allocate it on the stack, as this might take longer than the life of the calling function to complete!
/// An asyncIo.Queue must be specified. The newly-created task will be added to it when it completes its work.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `asyncio`: a pointer to an asyncIo.AsyncIo structure.
///   - `ptr`: a pointer to a buffer to read data into.
///   - `offset`: the position to start reading in the data source.
///   - `size`: the number of bytes to read from the data source.
///   - `queue`: a queue to add the new asyncIo.AsyncIo to.
///   - `userdata`: an app-defined pointer that will be provided with the task results.
///
/// - **Returns:** true on success or false on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** asyncIo.AsyncIo.write
/// - **See also:** asyncIo.createQueue
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn readAsyncIo(asyncio: ?AsyncIo, ptr: ?*anyopaque, offset: u64, size: u64, queue: ?AsyncIoQueue, userdata: ?*anyopaque) Error!void {
    if (!c.SDL_ReadAsyncIO(if (asyncio) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, @ptrCast(ptr), offset, size, if (queue) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, @ptrCast(userdata))) return error.SdlFailure;
}

/// Read from a data source.
///
/// This function reads up `size` bytes from the data source to the area pointed at by `ptr`. This function may read less bytes than requested.
/// This function will return zero when the data stream is completely read, and ioStream.IoStream.getStatus() will return ioStream.IoStatus.eof. If zero is returned and the stream is not at EOF, ioStream.IoStream.getStatus() will return a different error value and error_.get() will offer a human-readable message.
/// A request for zero bytes on a valid stream will return zero immediately without accessing the stream, so the stream status (EOF, err, etc) will not change.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `context`: a pointer to an ioStream.IoStream structure.
///   - `ptr`: a pointer to a buffer to read data into.
///
/// - **Returns:** the number of bytes read, or 0 on end of file or other failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** Do not use the same ioStream.IoStream from two threads at once.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** ioStream.IoStream.write
/// - **See also:** ioStream.IoStream.getStatus
inline fn readIo(context: ?IoStream, ptr: []u8) c_ulong {
    return c.SDL_ReadIO(if (context) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, @ptrCast(ptr.ptr), @intCast(ptr.len));
}

/// Read all the output from a process.
///
/// If a process was created with I/O enabled, you can use this function to read the output. This function blocks until the process is complete, capturing all output, and providing the process exit code.
/// The data is allocated with a zero byte at the end (null terminated) for convenience. This extra byte is not included in the value reported via `datasize`.
/// The returned sentinel slice is allocated with the caller-provided allocator.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `process_2`: The process to read.
///   - `exitcode`: a pointer filled in with the process exit code if the process has exited, may be NULL.
///
/// - **Returns:** the data or NULL on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** This function is not thread safe.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** process.create
/// - **See also:** process.createWithProperties
/// - **See also:** process.Process.deinit
inline fn readProcess(allocator_: std.mem.Allocator, process_2: ?Process, exitcode: ?*c_int) Error![:0]u8 {
    var byte_count: usize = 0;
    const result = c.SDL_ReadProcess(if (process_2) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, &byte_count, @ptrCast(exitcode)) orelse return error.SdlFailure;
    defer c.SDL_free(result);
    const source: [*]const u8 = @ptrCast(result);
    const copy = allocator_.allocSentinel(u8, byte_count, 0) catch return error.OutOfMemory;
    @memcpy(copy, source[0..byte_count]);
    return copy;
}

/// Named output values.
const ReadS16BeResult = struct {
    /// Output `value`.
    value: i16,
};

/// Use this function to read 16 bits of big-endian data from an ioStream.IoStream and return in native format.
///
/// SDL byteswaps the data only if necessary, so the data returned will be in the native byte order.
/// This function will return false when the data stream is completely read, and ioStream.IoStream.getStatus() will return ioStream.IoStatus.eof. If false is returned and the stream is not at EOF, ioStream.IoStream.getStatus() will return a different error value and error_.get() will offer a human-readable message.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `src`: the stream from which to read data.
///
/// - **Returns:** true on successful read or false on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** Do not use the same ioStream.IoStream from two threads at once.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// Returns named output values.
inline fn readS16Be(src: ?IoStream) ?ReadS16BeResult {
    var value_raw: @typeInfo(@typeInfo(@TypeOf(c.SDL_ReadS16BE)).@"fn".params[1].type.?).pointer.child = undefined;
    if (!c.SDL_ReadS16BE(if (src) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, &value_raw)) return null;
    return ReadS16BeResult{
        .value = value_raw,
    };
}

