/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
inline fn rectsEqual(a: ?*const Rect, b: ?*const Rect) bool {
    return c.SDL_RectsEqual(@ptrCast(a), @ptrCast(b));
}

/// Determine whether two floating point rectangles are equal, within some given epsilon.
///
/// Rectangles are considered equal if both are not NULL and each of their x, y, width and height are within `epsilon` of each other. If you don't know what value to use for `epsilon`, you should call the rect.rectsEqualFloat function instead.
