/// Update the screen with any rendering performed since the previous call.
///
/// SDL's rendering functions operate on a backbuffer; that is, calling a rendering function such as render.Renderer.renderLine() does not directly put a line on the screen, but rather updates the backbuffer. As such, you compose your entire scene and *present* the composed backbuffer to the screen as a complete picture.
