/// Please note, that in case of rendering to a texture - there is **no need** to call `render.Renderer.renderPresent` after drawing needed objects to a texture, and should not be done; you are only required to change back the rendering target to default via `render.Renderer.setRenderTarget(renderer, NULL)` afterwards, as textures by themselves do not have a concept of backbuffers. Calling render.Renderer.renderPresent while rendering to a texture will fail.
