/// Seek within an ioStream.IoStream data stream.
///
/// This function seeks to byte `offset`, relative to `whence`.
/// `whence` may be any of the following values:
/// - `ioStream.IoWhence.set`: seek from the beginning of data
/// - `ioStream.IoWhence.cur`: seek relative to current read point
/// - `ioStream.IoWhence.end`: seek relative to the end of data
/// If this stream can not seek, it will return -1.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `context`: a pointer to an ioStream.IoStream structure.
///   - `offset`: an offset in bytes, relative to `whence` location; can be negative.
///   - `whence`: any of `ioStream.IoWhence.set`, `ioStream.IoWhence.cur`, `ioStream.IoWhence.end`.
///
/// - **Returns:** the final offset in the data stream after the seek or -1 on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** Do not use the same ioStream.IoStream from two threads at once.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** ioStream.IoStream.tell
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn seekIo(context: ?IoStream, offset: i64, whence: IoWhence) Error!i64 {
    const result = c.SDL_SeekIO(if (context) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, offset, @intCast(@intFromEnum(whence)));
    if (result < 0) return error.SdlFailure;
    return result;
}

