/// When this surface is blitted, during the blit operation the source alpha value is modulated by this alpha value according to the following formula:
/// `srcA = srcA * (alpha / 255)`
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `surface_2`: the surface.Surface structure to update.
///   - `alpha`: the alpha value multiplied into blit operations.
///
/// - **Returns:** true on success or false on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** This function can be called on different threads with different surfaces.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** surface.getAlphaMod
/// - **See also:** surface.setColorMod
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn setSurfaceAlphaMod(surface_2: ?*Surface, alpha: u8) Error!void {
    if (!c.SDL_SetSurfaceAlphaMod(@ptrCast(surface_2), alpha)) return error.SdlFailure;
}

/// Set the blend mode used for blit operations.
///
/// To copy a surface to another surface (or texture) without blending with the existing data, the blendmode of the SOURCE surface should be set to `blendmode.blend_mode_none`.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `surface_2`: the surface.Surface structure to update.
///   - `blend_mode`: the blendmode.BlendMode to use for blit blending.
///
/// - **Returns:** true on success or false on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** This function can be called on different threads with different surfaces.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** surface.getBlendMode
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn setSurfaceBlendMode(surface_2: ?*Surface, blend_mode: BlendMode) Error!void {
    if (!c.SDL_SetSurfaceBlendMode(@ptrCast(surface_2), blend_mode)) return error.SdlFailure;
}

/// Set the clipping rectangle for a surface.
///
/// When `surface_2` is the destination of a blit, only the area within the clip rectangle is drawn into.
/// Note that blits are automatically clipped to the edges of the source and destination surfaces.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `surface_2`: the surface.Surface structure to be clipped.
///   - `rect_2`: the rect.Rect structure representing the clipping rectangle, or NULL to disable clipping.
///
/// - **Returns:** true if the rectangle intersects the surface, otherwise false and blits will be completely clipped.
/// - **Thread safety:** This function can be called on different threads with different surfaces.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** surface.getClipRect
inline fn setSurfaceClipRect(surface_2: ?*Surface, rect_2: ?*const Rect) bool {
    return c.SDL_SetSurfaceClipRect(@ptrCast(surface_2), @ptrCast(rect_2));
}

/// Set the color key (transparent pixel) in a surface.
///
/// The color key defines a pixel value that will be treated as transparent in a blit. For example, one can use this to specify that cyan pixels should be considered transparent, and therefore not rendered.
/// It is a pixel of the format used by the surface, as generated by pixels.mapRgb().
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `surface_2`: the surface.Surface structure to update.
///   - `enabled`: true to enable color key, false to disable color key.
