///
/// - **Returns:** true on success or false on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** This function can be called on different threads with different surfaces.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** surface.getColorKey
/// - **See also:** surface.setRle
/// - **See also:** surface.hasColorKey
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn setSurfaceColorKey(surface_2: ?*Surface, enabled: bool, key: u32) Error!void {
    if (!c.SDL_SetSurfaceColorKey(@ptrCast(surface_2), enabled, key)) return error.SdlFailure;
}

/// Set an additional color value multiplied into blit operations.
///
/// When this surface is blitted, during the blit operation each source color channel is modulated by the appropriate color value according to the following formula:
/// `srcC = srcC * (color / 255)`
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `surface_2`: the surface.Surface structure to update.
