/// Request that the window's fullscreen state be changed.
///
/// By default a window in fullscreen state uses borderless fullscreen desktop mode, but a specific exclusive display mode can be set using video.Window.setFullscreenMode().
/// On some windowing systems this request is asynchronous and the new fullscreen state may not have have been applied immediately upon the return of this function. If an immediate change is required, call video.Window.sync() to block until the changes have taken effect.
/// When the window state changes, an events.EventType.window_enter_fullscreen or events.EventType.window_leave_fullscreen event will be emitted. Note that, as this is just a request, it can be denied by the windowing system.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `window`: the window to change.
///   - `fullscreen`: true for fullscreen mode, false for windowed mode.
///
/// - **Returns:** true on success or false on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** This function should only be called on the main thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** video.Window.getFullscreenMode
/// - **See also:** video.Window.setFullscreenMode
/// - **See also:** video.Window.sync
/// - **See also:** video.WindowFlags.fullscreen
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn setWindowFullscreen(window: ?Window, fullscreen: bool) Error!void {
    if (!c.SDL_SetWindowFullscreen(if (window) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null, fullscreen)) return error.SdlFailure;
}

/// Set the display mode to use when a window is visible and fullscreen.
///
/// This only affects the display mode used when the window is fullscreen. To change the window size when the window is not fullscreen, use video.Window.setSize().
/// If the window is currently in the fullscreen state, this request is asynchronous on some windowing systems and the new mode dimensions may not be applied immediately upon the return of this function. If an immediate change is required, call video.Window.sync() to block until the changes have taken effect.
/// When the new mode takes effect, an events.EventType.window_resized and/or an events.EventType.window_pixel_size_changed event will be emitted with the new mode dimensions.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `window`: the window to affect.
