/// - **See also:** mutex.Semaphore.wait
/// - **See also:** mutex.Semaphore.waitTimeout
inline fn signalSemaphore(sem: ?Semaphore) void {
    c.SDL_SignalSemaphore(if (sem) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null);
}

/// Compute the sine of `x`.
///
/// Domain: `-INF <= x <= INF`
/// Range: `-1 <= y <= 1`
/// This function operates on double-precision floating point values, use stdinc.sinf for single-precision floats.
/// This function may use a different approximation across different versions, platforms and configurations. i.e, it can return a different value given the same input on different machines or operating systems, or if SDL is updated.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `x`: floating point value, in radians.
///
/// - **Returns:** sine of `x`.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** stdinc.sinf
/// - **See also:** stdinc.asin
/// - **See also:** stdinc.cos
inline fn sin(x: f64) f64 {
    return c.SDL_sin(x);
}

/// Compute the sine of `x`.
