}

/// This works exactly like sscanf() but doesn't require access to a C runtime.
///
/// Scan a string, matching a format string, converting each '' item and storing it to pointers provided through variable arguments.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `text`: the string to scan. Must not be NULL.
///   - `fmt`: a printf-style format string. Must not be NULL.
///   - `...`: a list of pointers to values to be filled in with scanned items.
///
/// - **Returns:** the number of items that matched the format string.
/// - **Thread safety:** It is safe to call this function from any thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
inline fn sscanf(text: [:0]const u8, comptime format: [:0]const u8, args: anytype) c_int {
    return @call(.auto, c.SDL_sscanf, .{ @as(@typeInfo(@TypeOf(c.SDL_sscanf)).@"fn".params[0].type.?, @ptrCast(text.ptr)), @as(@typeInfo(@TypeOf(c.SDL_sscanf)).@"fn".params[1].type.?, format.ptr) } ++ args);
}

/// Start accepting Unicode text input events in a window.
///
/// This function will enable text input (events.EventType.text_input and events.EventType.text_editing events) in the specified window. Please use this function paired with video.Window.stopTextInput().
/// Text input events are not received by default.
/// On some platforms using this function shows the screen keyboard and/or activates an IME, which can prevent some key press events from being passed through.
///
/// - **Parameters:**
///   - `window`: the window to enable text input.
///
/// - **Returns:** true on success or false on failure; call error_.get() for more information.
/// - **Thread safety:** This function should only be called on the main thread.
/// - **Since:** This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.
/// - **See also:** video.Window.setTextInputArea
/// - **See also:** video.Window.startTextInputWithProperties
/// - **See also:** video.Window.stopTextInput
/// - **See also:** video.Window.textInputActive
///
/// Returns `error.SdlFailure` when SDL reports failure.
inline fn startTextInput(window: ?Window) Error!void {
    if (!c.SDL_StartTextInput(if (window) |resource| @ptrCast(resource.value) else null)) return error.SdlFailure;
}

/// Start accepting Unicode text input events in a window, with properties describing the input.
///
/// This function will enable text input (events.EventType.text_input and events.EventType.text_editing events) in the specified window. Please use this function paired with video.Window.stopTextInput().
/// Text input events are not received by default.
/// On some platforms using this function shows the screen keyboard and/or activates an IME, which can prevent some key press events from being passed through.
/// These are the supported properties:
/// - `keyboard.prop_text_input_type_number` - an keyboard.TextInputType value that describes text being input, defaults to keyboard.TextInputType.text.
/// - `keyboard.prop_text_input_capitalization_number` - an keyboard.Capitalization value that describes how text should be capitalized, defaults to keyboard.Capitalization.sentences for normal text entry, keyboard.Capitalization.words for keyboard.TextInputType.text_name, and keyboard.Capitalization.none for e-mail addresses, usernames, and passwords.
/// - `keyboard.prop_text_input_autocorrect_boolean` - true to enable auto completion and auto correction, defaults to true.
/// - `keyboard.prop_text_input_multiline_boolean` - true if multiple lines of text are allowed. This defaults to true if hints.hint_return_key_hides_ime is "0" or is not set, and defaults to false if hints.hint_return_key_hides_ime is "1".
/// On Android you can directly specify the input type:
